title: Setup's first step, building the Docker container, sends the reader to 'bash/docker.sh', which is not in the repository.
pid: 0126cbac-d8a3-40be-ac7c-8868412858be
body: |2-
  'setup.org' says "See the image and mounts documented in
  ../bash/docker.sh" to build and to start the container, and
  'usage.org' says the same; 'bash/' has no such file. 'nvim/README.org'
  names 'coding-advice/docker.org' as describing the image, and no page
  in 'docs/' links that. The page also says "Please ask an AI for help
  setting it up." Here the reader without one stops for good.
  Change: put the commands that build, start and enter the container
  on the page itself, or link the file that holds them now.
